        "original_id": "5fff5f58-1716-5d97-b2d7-d4939324c1dd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charlie Ross, Gregg Harper, Tom Harkin, George Miller\n- Places: Mississippi, Mississippi's 3rd congressional district, Rankin County\n- Roles: U.S. Representative, state senator, Republican Chairman, committee chair, ranking member\n- Legislation: Keeping All Students Safe Act\n\nFacts:\n- In 2008, Charlie Ross ran for Congress in Mississippi's 3rd congressional district and lost the Republican primary to Rankin County Republican Chairman Gregg Harper.\n- Gregory Livingston Harper was born on June 1, 1956.\n- Gregg Harper has served as the U.S. Representative for Mississippi's 3rd congressional district since 2009.\n- The Keeping All Students Safe Act bills were primarily sponsored by Senator Tom Harkin, Congressman George Miller, and Congressman Gregg Harper.\n- Tom Harkin was Chair of the Senate Health, Education, Labor, and Pensions Committee when he sponsored the Keeping All Students Safe Act bills.\n- George Miller was Ranking Member of the House Education and Workforce Committee when he sponsored the Keeping All Students Safe Act bills.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
